IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 22 -- what the constitution of a company must state, the notice of a change in the number of members, the offence of not giving it,
-- the declaration of the number of shares a subscriber agrees to take, what "limited" means for a company limited by shares, and where the signed copy is kept. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Division 2 (s 23 on) is outside this part's range.
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".
-- A company limited both by shares and by guarantee is not one of the kinds paragraphs (b) to (e) name (s 17(5) bars registering one): those paragraphs answer `NOTHING` for it.

§ `Section 22(1): what the constitution must comply with, be dated and state`

DECLARE `s 22(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 22(1)(a) the name of the company`
    `s 22(1)(b) that the liability of the members is limited`
    `s 22(1)(c) that the liability of the members is limited and that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up`
    `s 22(1)(d) that the liability of the members is unlimited`
    `s 22(1)(e) the number of members with which the company is applying to be registered`
    `s 22(1)(f) the full names, addresses and occupations of the subscribers to the constitution of the company`
    `s 22(1)(g) that the subscribers are desirous of being formed into a company in pursuance of the constitution`
    `s 22(1) another matter`

-- Each paragraph (b) to (e) opens with "if the company is ...": a duty whose "if" gate is unmet answers JUST FALSE (the provision's own question; marginal reading (a)).
-- src:4078 | 22.—(1) The constitution of every company must comply with
-- src:4079 | such requirements as may be prescribed, must be dated and must
-- src:4080 | state, in addition to other requirements —
-- src:4082 | (a) the name of the company;
-- src:4087 | (b) if the company is a company limited by shares — that the
-- src:4088 | liability of the members is limited;
-- src:4090 | (c) if the company is a company limited by guarantee — that
-- src:4091 | the liability of the members is limited and that each
-- src:4092 | member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the
-- src:4093 | company, in the event of its being wound up while he or
-- src:4094 | she is a member or within one year after he or she ceases to
-- src:4095 | be a member, for payment of the debts and liabilities of the
-- src:4096 | company contracted before he or she ceases to be a
-- src:4097 | member and of the costs, charges and expenses of winding
-- src:4098 | up and for adjustment of the rights of the contributories
-- src:4099 | among themselves, such amount as may be required not
-- src:4100 | exceeding a specified amount;
-- src:4102 | (d) if the company is an unlimited company — that the
-- src:4103 | liability of the members is unlimited;
-- src:4105 | (e) if the company is an unlimited company or a company
-- src:4106 | limited by guarantee — the number of members with
-- src:4107 | which the company is applying to be registered;
-- src:4109 | (f) the full names, addresses and occupations of the
-- src:4110 | subscribers to the constitution of the company; and
-- src:4112 | (g) that such subscribers are desirous of being formed into a
-- src:4113 | company in pursuance of the constitution and (where the
-- src:4114 | company is to have a share capital) respectively agree to
-- src:4115 | take the number of shares in the capital of the company set
-- src:4116 | out opposite their respective names.
@ref s 22(1) (src:4078-4116)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 22(1) matter`
      liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the constitution must state the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 22(1)(a) the name of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 22(1)(f) the full names, addresses and occupations of the subscribers to the constitution of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 22(1)(g) that the subscribers are desirous of being formed into a company in pursuance of the constitution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 22(1)(b) that the liability of the members is limited` THEN
        (CONSIDER liability
         WHEN `limited by shares` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `limited by shares and by guarantee` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraphs name a company limited by shares, a company limited by guarantee and an unlimited company; the text names no statement for a company limited both by shares and by guarantee
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the company is a company limited by shares -- that the liability of the members is limited" (an "if" gate unmet on a duty: the provision's own question)
    WHEN `s 22(1)(c) that the liability of the members is limited and that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up` THEN
        (CONSIDER liability
         WHEN `limited by guarantee` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `limited by shares and by guarantee` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): as for paragraph (b)
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) if the company is a company limited by guarantee -- that the liability of the members is limited and that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company" (an "if" gate unmet on a duty)
    WHEN `s 22(1)(d) that the liability of the members is unlimited` THEN
        (CONSIDER liability
         WHEN `unlimited` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `limited by shares and by guarantee` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): as for paragraph (b)
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) if the company is an unlimited company -- that the liability of the members is unlimited" (an "if" gate unmet on a duty)
    WHEN `s 22(1)(e) the number of members with which the company is applying to be registered` THEN
        (CONSIDER liability
         WHEN `unlimited` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `limited by guarantee` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `limited by shares and by guarantee` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): as for paragraph (b)
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) if the company is an unlimited company or a company limited by guarantee -- the number of members with which the company is applying to be registered" (an "if" gate unmet on a duty)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the constitution "must state, in addition to other requirements"; the other requirements are prescribed elsewhere

-- The constitution complies when it meets the prescribed requirements, is dated, and states every matter that applies to the company.
-- The helper holds the conjunction (it is true when every requirement that applies to the company's kind is met).
-- src:4078 | 22.—(1) The constitution of every company must comply with
-- src:4079 | such requirements as may be prescribed, must be dated and must
-- src:4080 | state, in addition to other requirements —
-- src:4082 | (a) the name of the company;
-- src:4087 | (b) if the company is a company limited by shares — that the
-- src:4088 | liability of the members is limited;
-- src:4090 | (c) if the company is a company limited by guarantee — that
-- src:4091 | the liability of the members is limited and that each
-- src:4092 | member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the
-- src:4093 | company, in the event of its being wound up while he or
-- src:4094 | she is a member or within one year after he or she ceases to
-- src:4095 | be a member, for payment of the debts and liabilities of the
-- src:4096 | company contracted before he or she ceases to be a
-- src:4097 | member and of the costs, charges and expenses of winding
-- src:4098 | up and for adjustment of the rights of the contributories
-- src:4099 | among themselves, such amount as may be required not
-- src:4100 | exceeding a specified amount;
-- src:4102 | (d) if the company is an unlimited company — that the
-- src:4103 | liability of the members is unlimited;
-- src:4105 | (e) if the company is an unlimited company or a company
-- src:4106 | limited by guarantee — the number of members with
-- src:4107 | which the company is applying to be registered;
-- src:4109 | (f) the full names, addresses and occupations of the
-- src:4110 | subscribers to the constitution of the company; and
-- src:4112 | (g) that such subscribers are desirous of being formed into a
-- src:4113 | company in pursuance of the constitution and (where the
-- src:4114 | company is to have a share capital) respectively agree to
-- src:4115 | take the number of shares in the capital of the company set
-- src:4116 | out opposite their respective names.
@ref s 22(1) (src:4078-4116)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the constitution complies with such requirements as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution is dated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states the name of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that the liability of the members is limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that the liability of the members is unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states the number of members with which the company is applying to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states the full names, addresses and occupations of the subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that the subscribers are desirous of being formed into a company in pursuance of the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that the subscribers respectively agree to take the number of shares in the capital of the company set out opposite their respective names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) every requirement that applies to the company is met` MEANS
        `the constitution complies with such requirements as may be prescribed`
    AND `the constitution is dated`
    AND `the constitution states the name of the company`
    AND ((NOT (liability EQUALS `limited by shares`)) OR `the constitution states that the liability of the members is limited`)
    AND ((NOT (liability EQUALS `limited by guarantee`)) OR (`the constitution states that the liability of the members is limited` AND `the constitution states that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up`))
    AND ((NOT (liability EQUALS `unlimited`)) OR `the constitution states that the liability of the members is unlimited`)
    AND ((liability EQUALS `limited by shares`) OR `the constitution states the number of members with which the company is applying to be registered`)
    AND `the constitution states the full names, addresses and occupations of the subscribers`
    AND `the constitution states that the subscribers are desirous of being formed into a company in pursuance of the constitution`
    AND ((NOT `the company is to have a share capital`) OR `the constitution states that the subscribers respectively agree to take the number of shares in the capital of the company set out opposite their respective names`)

-- src:4078 | 22.—(1) The constitution of every company must comply with
-- src:4079 | such requirements as may be prescribed, must be dated and must
-- src:4080 | state, in addition to other requirements —
-- src:4082 | (a) the name of the company;
-- src:4087 | (b) if the company is a company limited by shares — that the
-- src:4088 | liability of the members is limited;
-- src:4090 | (c) if the company is a company limited by guarantee — that
-- src:4091 | the liability of the members is limited and that each
-- src:4092 | member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the
-- src:4093 | company, in the event of its being wound up while he or
-- src:4094 | she is a member or within one year after he or she ceases to
-- src:4095 | be a member, for payment of the debts and liabilities of the
-- src:4096 | company contracted before he or she ceases to be a
-- src:4097 | member and of the costs, charges and expenses of winding
-- src:4098 | up and for adjustment of the rights of the contributories
-- src:4099 | among themselves, such amount as may be required not
-- src:4100 | exceeding a specified amount;
-- src:4102 | (d) if the company is an unlimited company — that the
-- src:4103 | liability of the members is unlimited;
-- src:4105 | (e) if the company is an unlimited company or a company
-- src:4106 | limited by guarantee — the number of members with
-- src:4107 | which the company is applying to be registered;
-- src:4109 | (f) the full names, addresses and occupations of the
-- src:4110 | subscribers to the constitution of the company; and
-- src:4112 | (g) that such subscribers are desirous of being formed into a
-- src:4113 | company in pursuance of the constitution and (where the
-- src:4114 | company is to have a share capital) respectively agree to
-- src:4115 | take the number of shares in the capital of the company set
-- src:4116 | out opposite their respective names.
@ref s 22(1) (src:4078-4116)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the constitution complies with such requirements as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution is dated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states the name of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that the liability of the members is limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that the liability of the members is unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states the number of members with which the company is applying to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states the full names, addresses and occupations of the subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that the subscribers are desirous of being formed into a company in pursuance of the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution states that the subscribers respectively agree to take the number of shares in the capital of the company set out opposite their respective names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the constitution complies with the subsection` MEANS
    IF liability EQUALS `limited by shares and by guarantee`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraphs name a company limited by shares, a company limited by guarantee and an unlimited company; the text names no requirement for a company limited both by shares and by guarantee
    ELSE (IF `s 22(1) every requirement that applies to the company is met` liability `the constitution complies with such requirements as may be prescribed` `the constitution is dated` `the constitution states the name of the company` `the constitution states that the liability of the members is limited` `the constitution states that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up` `the constitution states that the liability of the members is unlimited` `the constitution states the number of members with which the company is applying to be registered` `the constitution states the full names, addresses and occupations of the subscribers` `the constitution states that the subscribers are desirous of being formed into a company in pursuance of the constitution` `the company is to have a share capital` `the constitution states that the subscribers respectively agree to take the number of shares in the capital of the company set out opposite their respective names`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The constitution of every company must comply with such requirements as may be prescribed, must be dated and must state, in addition to other requirements -- (a) ...; (g) that such subscribers are desirous of being formed into a company ... and (where the company is to have a share capital) respectively agree to take the number of shares" (a duty not fully met: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 22(1AA) and (1AB): the notice of a change in the number of members, and the offence`

-- src:4120 | (1AA) Where a company to which subsection (1)(e) applies
-- src:4121 | changes the number of its members with which it is registered, the
-- src:4122 | company must, within 14 days after the occurrence of such change,
-- src:4123 | lodge with the Registrar a notice of the change in the prescribed form.
@ref s 22(1AA) (src:4120-4123)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the company changes the number of its members with which it is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1AA) the company must lodge with the Registrar a notice of the change` MEANS
    IF liability EQUALS `unlimited` OR liability EQUALS `limited by guarantee`
    THEN (IF `the company changes the number of its members with which it is registered`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company to which subsection (1)(e) applies changes the number of its members with which it is registered, the company must ... lodge with the Registrar a notice of the change" (a duty whose "where" gate is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "a company to which subsection (1)(e) applies", an unlimited company or a company limited by guarantee; the text says nothing of any other company

-- src:4120 | (1AA) Where a company to which subsection (1)(e) applies
-- src:4121 | changes the number of its members with which it is registered, the
-- src:4122 | company must, within 14 days after the occurrence of such change,
-- src:4123 | lodge with the Registrar a notice of the change in the prescribed form.
@ref s 22(1AA) (src:4120-4123)
GIVEN `the date of the change in the number of its members` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice of the change in the prescribed form was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1AA) the company lodged the notice of the change in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the notice of the change in the prescribed form was lodged with the Registrar` AT LEAST `the date of the change in the number of its members` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the change in the number of its members` `the date the notice of the change in the prescribed form was lodged with the Registrar` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the occurrence of such change, lodge with the Registrar a notice of the change in the prescribed form" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); the day of the change is in time, fork line F-H-P2)

-- src:4127 | (1AB) If default is made by a company in complying with
-- src:4128 | subsection (1AA), the company and every officer of the company
-- src:4129 | who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be
-- src:4134 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a
-- src:4135 | default penalty.
@ref s 22(1AB) (src:4127-4135)
GIVEN `default is made by the company in complying with subsection (1AA)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1AB) the company or officer in default is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made by the company in complying with subsection (1AA)` AND `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line F-H-S2): "If default is made by a company in complying with subsection (1AA), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts

-- src:4127 | (1AB) If default is made by a company in complying with
-- src:4128 | subsection (1AA), the company and every officer of the company
-- src:4129 | who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be
-- src:4134 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a
-- src:4135 | default penalty.
@ref s 22(1AB) (src:4127-4135)
GIVEN `default is made by the company in complying with subsection (1AA)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 22(1AB) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 22(1AB) the company or officer in default is guilty of an offence` `default is made by the company in complying with subsection (1AA)` `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty": no imprisonment, and the default penalty is added to the fine
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- src:4139 | (1A) On 30 January 2006, any provision (or part thereof) then
-- src:4140 | subsisting in the constitution of any company which states —
-- src:4142 | (a) the amount of share capital with which the company
-- src:4143 | proposes to be or is registered; or
-- src:4145 | (b) the division of the share capital of the company into shares
-- src:4146 | of a fixed amount,
-- src:4148 | is, insofar as it relates to the matters referred to in either or both of
-- src:4149 | paragraphs (a) and (b), deemed to be deleted.
@ref s 22(1A) (src:4139-4149)
GIVEN `the provision was then subsisting in the constitution of the company on 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the amount of share capital with which the company proposes to be or is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the division of the share capital of the company into shares of a fixed amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1A) the provision is deemed to be deleted, insofar as it relates to those matters` MEANS
    IF NOT `the provision was then subsisting in the constitution of the company on 30 January 2006`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On 30 January 2006, any provision (or part thereof) then subsisting in the constitution of any company" -- a failed "on" gate: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)
    ELSE (IF `it states the amount of share capital with which the company proposes to be or is registered` OR `it states the division of the share capital of the company into shares of a fixed amount`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any provision ... which states -- (a) the amount of share capital ...; or (b) the division of the share capital ... into shares of a fixed amount" -- a provision that states neither is outside the class the subsection deems deleted: a scope limit with no "only", the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); changed from JUST FALSE after the independent reader (wave-2 reader A, scenario 321), assumed, not ruled

§ `Section 22(2) to (4): the declaration of shares, "limited", and the signed copy`

-- src:4153 | (2) Each subscriber to the constitution must, if the company is to
-- src:4154 | have a share capital, make a declaration to the Registrar, either
-- src:4155 | personally or through a registered qualified individual authorised by
-- src:4156 | the subscriber, as to the number of shares (not being less than one)
-- src:4157 | that the subscriber agrees to take.
@ref s 22(2) (src:4153-4157)
GIVEN `the company is to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) the subscriber must make a declaration to the Registrar as to the number of shares the subscriber agrees to take` MEANS
    IF `the company is to have a share capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each subscriber to the constitution must, if the company is to have a share capital, make a declaration to the Registrar" (an "if" gate unmet on a duty: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- src:4153 | (2) Each subscriber to the constitution must, if the company is to
-- src:4154 | have a share capital, make a declaration to the Registrar, either
-- src:4155 | personally or through a registered qualified individual authorised by
-- src:4156 | the subscriber, as to the number of shares (not being less than one)
-- src:4157 | that the subscriber agrees to take.
@ref s 22(2) (src:4153-4157)
GIVEN `the declaration is made personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration is made through a registered qualified individual authorised by the subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) the declaration is made in a way the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the declaration is made personally` OR `the declaration is made through a registered qualified individual authorised by the subscriber`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make a declaration to the Registrar, either personally or through a registered qualified individual authorised by the subscriber" (a closed pair: "either ... or")

-- src:4153 | (2) Each subscriber to the constitution must, if the company is to
-- src:4154 | have a share capital, make a declaration to the Registrar, either
-- src:4155 | personally or through a registered qualified individual authorised by
-- src:4156 | the subscriber, as to the number of shares (not being less than one)
-- src:4157 | that the subscriber agrees to take.
@ref s 22(2) (src:4153-4157)
GIVEN `the number of shares the subscriber agrees to take` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) the number of shares the subscriber agrees to take is a number the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the number of shares the subscriber agrees to take` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as to the number of shares (not being less than one) that the subscriber agrees to take" (a flat negative)

-- src:4161 | (3) A statement in the constitution of a company limited by shares
-- src:4162 | that the liability of members is limited means that the liability of the
-- src:4163 | members is limited to the amount (if any) unpaid on the shares
-- src:4164 | respectively held by them.
@ref s 22(3) (src:4161-4164)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the constitution of the company states that the liability of members is limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount (if any) unpaid on the shares held by the member` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 22(3) the most the member is liable to contribute` MEANS
    IF liability EQUALS `limited by shares` AND `the constitution of the company states that the liability of members is limited`
    THEN JUST `the amount (if any) unpaid on the shares held by the member`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "A statement in the constitution of a company limited by shares that the liability of members is limited"; the text says nothing of any other statement or company

-- src:4168 | (4) A copy of the constitution, duly signed by the subscribers and
-- src:4169 | stating, if the company is to have a share capital, the number of shares
-- src:4170 | that each subscriber has agreed to take, must be kept at the registered
-- src:4171 | office of the company.
@ref s 22(4) (src:4168-4171)
GIVEN `the copy of the constitution is duly signed by the subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy states the number of shares that each subscriber has agreed to take` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is kept at the registered office of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(4) the copy of the constitution is kept as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the copy of the constitution is duly signed by the subscribers` AND ((NOT `the company is to have a share capital`) OR `the copy states the number of shares that each subscriber has agreed to take`) AND `the copy is kept at the registered office of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A copy of the constitution, duly signed by the subscribers and stating, if the company is to have a share capital, the number of shares that each subscriber has agreed to take, must be kept at the registered office of the company" (a duty not met: the provision's own question; the text names no bearer, no act and no time, so there is no regulative rule: NOTES.md, rules with no breach path)

§ `Regulative rules of s 22`

DECLARE `s 22 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 22(1AA) lodge with the Registrar a notice of the change in the number of members in the prescribed form`
    `s 22(2) make a declaration to the Registrar as to the number of shares the subscriber agrees to take`

-- A DEADLINE: "within 14 days after the occurrence of such change". The consequence the text states is the offence of s 22(1AB) (a fine of up to $2,000 and a default penalty).
-- src:4120 | (1AA) Where a company to which subsection (1)(e) applies
-- src:4121 | changes the number of its members with which it is registered, the
-- src:4122 | company must, within 14 days after the occurrence of such change,
-- src:4123 | lodge with the Registrar a notice of the change in the prescribed form.
@ref s 22(1AA) (src:4120-4123)
GIVEN bearer IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 22 act`
`s 22(1AA) rule: the company's duty to lodge a notice of the change in the number of members` MEANS
    PARTY bearer
    MUST `s 22(1AA) lodge with the Registrar a notice of the change in the number of members in the prescribed form`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY bearer BECAUSE "the company did not lodge a notice of the change in the prescribed form within 14 days, which is an offence under section 22(1AB)"

-- No time limit and no consequence stated: no breach path.
-- src:4153 | (2) Each subscriber to the constitution must, if the company is to
-- src:4154 | have a share capital, make a declaration to the Registrar, either
-- src:4155 | personally or through a registered qualified individual authorised by
-- src:4156 | the subscriber, as to the number of shares (not being less than one)
-- src:4157 | that the subscriber agrees to take.
@ref s 22(2) (src:4153-4157)
GIVEN bearer IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 22 act`
`s 22(2) rule: the subscriber's duty to make a declaration of the number of shares` MEANS
    PARTY bearer
    MUST `s 22(2) make a declaration to the Registrar as to the number of shares the subscriber agrees to take`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 22(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY bearer BECAUSE "the subscriber did not make a declaration to the Registrar as to the number of shares the subscriber agrees to take" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]
